# Source material is yours, not the repo's. The folder structure is tracked via
# .gitkeep; what you drop into it is not. This repo is public, and a knowledge
# base of transcripts and licensed research must not be published with it.
#
# Note the shape: excluding kb/files/** would exclude the directories too, and
# git will not descend into an excluded directory to re-include a file in it,
# so the .gitkeep negation would silently do nothing.
kb/files/*/*
!kb/files/*/.gitkeep
